&lt;p&gt;Data represents the voice of Airbnb’s users at scale. The Data Warehouse Infrastructure team is responsible for the foundational big data infrastructure, which is used by hundreds of engineers to collect, manage, and analyze data at scale. We are using open source technologies like Hadoop, Spark, Trino, Iceberg, Airflow etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, design, and implement Airbnb&#39;s next-generation big data compute platform to support data ETL, analytics, and machine learning initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and operate the platform, continually enhancing its reliability, performance, observability, and cost-efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce high-quality, maintainable, and self-documenting code, actively participating in code review processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to open-source software and drive meaningful industry impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
