&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The Authorization Infrastructure team builds and operates &lt;a href=&quot;https://medium.com/airbnb-engineering/himeji-a-scalable-centralized-system-for-authorization-at-airbnb-341664924574&quot;&gt;Himeji&lt;/a&gt;, the authorization system powering over 8 million authorization checks per second that underpins every access to data and resources at Airbnb. Our mission is to make authorization reliable, secure, and correct by default, removing the burden from every team to solve access from first principles. We are a high-impact, platform-focused team entering an inflection point: as AI agents become first-class principals across Airbnb&#39;s product surfaces, we are defining what secure-by-default authorization looks like for the AI era. Our north star: secure every identity, every action, every agent, making Airbnb&#39;s AI transformation trusted by default. You will partner closely with engineering teams across InfoSec, AI Infrastructure, Privacy, ML Infrastructure, and Airbnb&#39;s product platform to shape the authorization foundation the entire company relies on.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer on Authorization Infrastructure, you will own the long-term technical strategy and architectural direction of the authorization platform, defining how it evolves to support AI-era patterns including natural language policies, contextual access decisions, and multi-principal agentic workflows. Success in this role means advancing Himeji&#39;s core architecture northstar, securing cross-team alignment on AI agent authorization, and establishing Airbnb-wide engineering standards for what &quot;paved path authorization&quot; looks like at every product surface. This is a rare opportunity to operate at the intersection of foundational infrastructure and cutting-edge AI security for one of the world&#39;s most trusted platforms.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, development, and evolution of Airbnb’s authorization platform, shaping roadmap, architecture, and delivery while ensuring high reliability, performance, and operational excellence at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive the next generation of authorization for AI and agentic workflows, defining clear access models for agents and building systems that enforce correctness, least-privilege access, and end-to-end auditability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with InfoSec, AI/ML Infra, Product, Privacy, and Data teams to align on authorization standards and drive adoption across the platform. This includes integrating authorization deeply into data access paths, improving correctness, coverage, and developer experience across the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead design and execution of high-impact, high-risk authorization initiatives across multiple teams and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and uphold engineering standards through design reviews, technical leadership, and mentorship of senior engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software engineering experience, with significant time designing and operating large-scale, high-reliability distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in authorization, access control, or identity systems, including policy models, permission frameworks, or trust infrastructure at production scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of owning complex, cross-organizational technical strategy: authoring foundational RFCs, building alignment across teams with competing priorities, and making high-stakes architectural commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing engineering standards beyond your immediate team, at the engineering council, org-wide, or across platform and product organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and technical leadership skills, with the ability to engage effectively across engineering, security, product leadership, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI agent architectures and the security and authorization challenges they introduce is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
