&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;MKTQ227R26&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director of Internal Communications, you&#39;ll keep thousands of Bricksters informed, aligned, and connected to our mission, our products, and our culture as we scale. You&#39;ll own company-wide communications, run our most important internal moments, and serve as a trusted partner to our founders and executive team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a strategic, hands-on role for a leader who thrives in fast-moving environments, knows how to cut through noise, and can translate technical topics and business priorities into clear, compelling narratives that resonate across a global organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive &amp;amp; Founder Communications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted communications advisor to Databricks&#39; leaders, providing strategic counsel and content development for internal audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop high-impact content, talking points, and presentations for company-wide moments including All Hands, Company Kickoff, and leadership forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with leadership to distill complex ideas — technical, strategic, and organizational — into narratives that land with employees at every level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company-Wide Internal Communications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Databricks&#39; internal communications strategy: All Hands, Company Kickoff, org announcements, and major company updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure employees always understand where the company is going, why it matters, and how their work connects to our mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate messaging across leaders to deliver clarity and consistency at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with across departments to align internal and external narratives, especially around major announcements, product launches, and organizational changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with production teams for live and recorded events such as All Hands, Company Kickoffs, etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead change communications for key initiatives, helping employees navigate transitions with clarity and confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support our Chief People Officer and Chief Revenue Officer executive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in internal or executive communications, preferably in enterprise software, cloud, or AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record supporting founders and C-level executives with speechwriting, messaging, and high-stakes internal events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional storytelling skills — able to simplify complex topics and write in a range of executive voices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to bring content to life across video, graphics, podcasts, agents, and written content.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning large-scale internal programs and content production (All Hands, Kickoffs, videos) for global, distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in high-visibility, fast-moving environments with multiple senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills with the ability to juggle competing priorities without dropping the ball.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Communications, English, Journalism, Marketing, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
