&lt;p&gt;Do you get excited about creating the best event experiences? Do you enjoy the fast-paced culture of a high-growth tech startup where you have the opportunity to directly influence the business&#39; success? The Senior Event Content Manager at Databricks will report to the Director, Event Marketing and guide the session content workstream for corporate events including Data + AI Summit. You will ensure the delivery of first-class, valuable, engaging, and high-impact session content, with a strong focus on operational excellence to achieve scalability. This role is open to remote work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the strategy and delivery of a high-quality session content experience for corporate events at Databricks that meet attendees&#39; educational needs and support Databricks&#39;s priorities and important messages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze content consumption and conversion to business to create and develop a content strategy. Partner with Product Marketing, Dev Rel, Partner Marketing, Industry Marketing and other stakeholders to help support event goals. Facilitate stakeholder input, summarize product information, identify dependencies and deliver a comprehensive roadmap for session content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Databrick&#39;s Dev Rel team to lead the OSS community to get state-of-the-art content submissions. Work with internal reviewers to build a strong community content agenda.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee all content operations including call for presentations, track organization, speaker/session selection, allocations, scheduling, track owner/speaker management and collaboration with the Event Tech team. Build out the speaker review process. Develop creative content methods of engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on event marcom, contributing to email and promotional comms, working closely with the web and event tech teams on session page design and execution and ensuring agreement on content deadlines to meet marcom/promo needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with logistics, AV and infrastructure teams to improve room and session sizes and ensure session room requirements, AV needs, wifi, room management, scanning, etc. are planned for&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the event teach team for implementation and management of event tech tools for content management, solving any unique challenges and ensuring data accuracy. Collaborate with Marcom team to ensure messaging and instructions on how to use the mobile app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee operational support for the content specialist contractor and vendor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create various reports that share key findings throughout content development and post-event cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong relationships with the event team and other cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in event content management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of event content pillars and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Efficient project management skills to build cohesive plans, and create agreement across groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic mindset relying on data to help drive the strategy; and proactively make recommendations on vision and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex projects with multiple stakeholders across the globe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the process and tools for content management. This includes the ability to learn new tools and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable presenting on a complex workstream but able to simplify for an executive audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Salesforce.com, Google Suite, Asana, Tableau, Marketo, Rainfocus, Swoogo, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
