&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sr. Events Marketing Manager - &lt;/strong&gt;Data + AI World Tour&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you get excited about creating the best-in-class event experiences that take operational excellence to the next level? Do you enjoy the fast-paced culture of high-growth tech companies where you have the opportunity to directly impact the business’ success? As a Sr. Event Marketing Manager at Databricks, you will support operations, strategy, and execution for our global Data + AI World Tour, This role transforms event operations from reactive to strategic, building scalable systems that enable best-in-class experiences while maintaining operational excellence across multiple global markets. This role will report to the VP of Global Events with a dotted line to the Principal Event Marketer for the World Tour Program&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outcomes: the impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scalable Operations&lt;/strong&gt;: Help establish repeatable systems and processes that enable Data + AI World Tour to scale across new markets without operational complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence: &lt;/strong&gt;Deliver flawless event execution with on-time, on-budget delivery across all milestones and deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Visibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide clear performance reporting that connects event metrics to business outcomes and informs future strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Facilitate seamless collaboration between global teams, agencies, and stakeholders that eliminates bottlenecks and accelerates execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget Efficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain financial accountability with zero budget overruns and optimized vendor relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;: Support regional teams with standardized tools and resources that ensure consistent event quality across all locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Trust: &lt;/strong&gt;Build confidence with marketing and sales leadership through reliable delivery and transparent communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of event marketing experience, driving demand to event programs in a B2B enterprise software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills with track record of delivering multiple concurrent projects on deadline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder global programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills with ability to lead cross-functional meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven capacity for exceptional customer service to internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized, detail-oriented, and self-directed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics-driven and be a strong analytical thinker with ability to utilize data to drive the success and the evolution of the conference.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Virtual event experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Google Suite, Marketo, Salesforce, Tableau, Asana, Rainfocus, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
