&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an IT Systems/Automation Engineer, you will be a core technical contributor on the IT Digital Employee Experience team at Databricks, owning and driving automation platforms and endpoint security programs that reduce friction across the company. This role requires a strong automation mindset, deep technical breadth across IT systems, and the ability to deliver high-quality, scalable solutions in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Impact You Will Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve our IT automation platform, serving as the subject matter expert and driving design, implementation, and improvement of automation workflows across IT and Security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and maintain the Mobile Security program, MDM configuration, and policy enforcement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver end-to-end automation solutions across onboarding/offboarding and security compliance workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional stakeholders across IAM, Security, Infrastructure, and Engineering to deliver impactful projects with real business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support M&amp;amp;A technical integrations by applying your automation skills to accelerate onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document solutions, train, and mentor junior engineers of the platforms you own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in IT systems engineering and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of delivering complex, multi-system automation projects with measurable business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong automation mindset: you don&#39;t just execute tasks, you architect scalable automated solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
