&lt;li&gt;Technical Fluency: Ability to engage deeply in architecture and integration discussions. You can identify hidden technical risks, assess complexity, and drive rigorous operational readiness planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence without Authority: Proven ability to build relationships across organizational boundaries and drive alignment among senior stakeholders with competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication Excellence: Ability to craft executive-ready narratives that crisp up complex tradeoffs into clear, actionable recommendations for leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilience in Ambiguity: Comfort with shifting specifications or standards; you create the conditions for engineering teams to remain productive and focused during periods of high ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execution Rigor: A default-to-action mindset with the ability to build and enforce the mechanisms (dashboards, cadences, checklists) required to maintain high-velocity execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, a related field or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
