&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in our San Francisco or New York City office. We are a hybrid environment that combines the energy and connections of being in the office with the benefits and flexibility of working from home. We currently require a minimum of three coordinated days in the office per week: Monday, Wednesday and Thursday. As a perk, we also have up to four weeks per year of fully remote work!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a portfolio of approximately 200 companies (Seed through Series B+), serving as the primary point of contact for founders, CFOs, and Chiefs of Staff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain deep awareness of each client&#39;s financial health, funding status, and growth trajectory to identify and address opportunities proactively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold operational excellence through rigorous Salesforce hygiene and proficiency in tools such as Vitally, Gong, Scratchpad, HEX, Looker and LogRocket.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Net Revenue Retention (NRR) through the proactive expansion of products, including credit card utilization, growing banking deposits, adoption of bill pay, invoicing and travel products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead deposit acquisition by capturing fresh capital during financing rounds through the strategic positioning of Brex&#39;s banking and treasury solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute competitive defense strategies to protect your book of business, cultivating relationships built on trust rather than simple cash incentives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner through strategic collaboration with cross-functional teams to deliver optimal solutions, products, and services to our clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize field engagement by targeting in-person interactions with customers by having in-person meetings and touch points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage event curation by hosting at least one monthly client event, such as intimate dinners, workout sessions, or other curated experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in relationship management, account management, sales, partnerships, or a similar role, preferably within the startup or finance ecosystem or saas or banking industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistent record of exceeding quota and delivering top performance in competitive sales environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build and maintain relationships with diverse stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and results-oriented mindset, with the ability to work independently and as a part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and project management skills, with the ability to multitask and prioritize effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze data and metrics to drive informed decisions and strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the startup ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
