&lt;p&gt;Instacart’s Strategic Partnerships team drives growth, accelerates strategic priorities, and unlocks new opportunities through high-impact partnerships across the technology ecosystem. We are hiring a Senior Manager, Product and Technology Partnerships to lead first-of-a-kind, product-led alliances that power our Enterprise business—including Retailer Storefronts, Fulfillment products, and in-store technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this highly visible role, you will design and execute partnership strategies, negotiate complex agreements, and own senior executive relationships across categories such as POS, loyalty, and e-commerce. You will work closely with Initiative leads (GMs), Product, Engineering, Finance, Legal, Solutions Architects, and Enterprise Leadership to bring partnerships from idea to launch and scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join an experienced, results-driven team that values strategic thinking, creativity, and data-informed decision-making. If you thrive in fast-paced, ambiguous environments, love building from 0-to-1, and enjoy collaborating cross-functionally to deliver measurable impact, this role offers a unique opportunity to shape Instacart’s next chapter. This role is based in Toronto, Canada, with flexibility across Canada in line with our Flex First approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Instacart’s B2B technology partnerships for Enterprise across Retailer Storefronts, Fulfillment products, and in-store technologies, from strategy through launch and ongoing growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, evaluate, and secure first-of-a-kind partnerships with key industry players; create and iterate the playbook for new partnership models and go-to-market motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and communicate clear partnership strategies and business cases that align with product roadmaps and company objectives, collaborating closely with Product and Engineering leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portfolio of partners end to end—sourcing, structuring, negotiating, signing, launching, and managing—while maintaining senior executive-level relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run recurring business reviews with partners to track performance, surface insights, and drive delivery of high-impact results for both Instacart and our partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in business development or partnerships within technology or closely related industries, with end-to-end ownership of complex, multi-stakeholder deals from sourcing through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success negotiating enterprise technology agreements (e.g., MSAs, SOWs, data/privacy addenda, commercial terms) in close partnership with Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience building and executing product and technology partnerships with enterprise platforms in POS, loyalty, e-commerce, or adjacent ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced analytical skills, including financial modeling and business case development to evaluate and optimize partnership impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with both software and hardware partnerships across the retail or in-store technology stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience in retail, grocery, or related enterprise technology domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or mentoring a lean team and influencing cross-functional stakeholders at the senior executive level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or equivalent advanced degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in fast-paced, ambiguous environments; highly curious, resourceful, and comfortable charting a course with limited precedent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
