&lt;p&gt;FoodStorm, Instacart’s order management platform for prepared foods and catering, powers seamless in-store operations and connects them to an exceptional online grocery experience. We are seeking a Senior Product Manager to lead FoodStorm’s in-store product strategy and deepen the connection between our retailer partners’ counters, kitchens, and digital storefronts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will partner closely with a global R&amp;amp;D team of about 50 cross-functional teammates, including roughly 20 engineers, spanning Melbourne, the United States, and Canada. You’ll collaborate with design, data, operations, and go-to-market teams across Instacart, as well as directly with North American retailers, to deliver products that drive measurable adoption, revenue, and shopper satisfaction at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to build at the speed of a scale-up with the reach of a market leader. If you thrive in fast-paced, highly collaborative environments and enjoy rolling up your sleeves to solve complex, real-world problems, we’d love to hear from you. The role is open to remote candidates in the US and Canada, with San Francisco as a preferred location for in-person collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy, roadmap, and execution for FoodStorm’s in-store experiences, bridging prepared foods and catering operations with Instacart’s online grocery ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate retailer and customer insights into clear problem statements, PRDs, and prioritized backlogs; drive delivery with an engineering team of 20+ using agile practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional alignment with design, analytics, operations, and adjacent platform teams to ship high-quality features end-to-end, from discovery through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success metrics, instrument products for analytics, run experiments, and use data to inform tradeoffs and rapidly improve business and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with North American retailers to pilot solutions in stores, gather feedback on the ground, and scale adoption across banners and locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage complex platform integrations (e.g., POS, payments, inventory, fulfillment) and ensure reliability, performance, privacy, and compliance in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
